@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.10.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.10.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.10.0 (2026-11-20): The generic code check is built and tested; story ST11_Check is Done. Also a correction to the single-source step record: while testing the check against the real chapter files I found that the chapter-code manifest has a wrapper (kind, deck, about, executed_with, library, examples) written by the generic deck builder from the examples module, so the step 1.0.0 manifest output was the wrong shape. Step 1.1.0 (new file) writes a plain examples list instead and leaves the manifest to the builder. The 1.0.0 file and its Done record stay as committed."""@en .

ex:TK11_Check_Build backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "08-tooling/code_check_v1_0_0.py: four conditions on a chapter source file: C1 examples list equals source in order, C2 each source slide has exactly one code box equal to the source code, C3 the page data holds the whole code string as the source has it, C4 setup plus code runs to the end. No chapter text. Accepts the examples list or the chapter-code manifest wrapper." .
ex:TK11_Check_Verify backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Logs in 08-tooling/code-source/logs_v1_0_0: check_toy_run.log (good toy passes all four; five broken copies, each refused under its own condition and named message), make_1_1_0_toy_run.log (two identical runs, the tab runs), check_old_decks_baseline.log (the existing chapter 10 and 11 decks 3.0.0: C2 fails on 18 of 18 and 19 of 19 code slides, C1 and C3 pass against the manifests 1.1.0 and pages 9.20.0). A first harness run had two wrong results, caused by my test (slide numbers not padded; a page check that accepted a prefix), and by a weak page condition; both fixed and rerun before this record. Run by the agent that wrote the tool, so not independent. Note: the tool counts 37 of 37 failing slides where my hand count said 35 of 37 split; the difference is that C2 also fails a slide whose single box holds extra set-up lines. The objective figure stays as measured by hand and the tool's figure is the one used from now on." .
ex:ST11_Check backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Criterion met; see its tasks." .
ex:TK11_Make_Verify backlog:hasAuditNote "Correction of 1.10.0: the manifest output tested here was the wrong shape (see the register comment); step 1.1.0 replaces it, tested in make_1_1_0_toy_run.log." .
ex:DoD11_ToolRun rdfs:comment "Run on 2026-11-20 also for the generic code check: 08-tooling/code-source/logs_v1_0_0/check_toy_run.log and make_1_1_0_toy_run.log." .
